    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0220" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg164"/>

                <head>No. 86.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nicholas
                            Fish to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 3, 1876</date>.
                        (Received October 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 495.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 478, inclosing the law
                    concerning the state’s right of supervision in the administration of property in
                    Catholic dioceses, I have now the honor to inclose herewith a copy and
                    translation of the royal decree concerning the exercise of the right of
                    supervision on the part of the state in the administration of property in
                    Catholic dioceses, dated 29th September last, and published in the official
                    gazette of September 30.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>NICHOLAS FISH.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d87-a1.xml" xpointer="d87-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
